WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.162
Marcus’s older daughter is 24, finished with school,

00:00:03.162 --> 00:00:06.324
working part time and living in another city.

00:00:06.324 --> 00:00:10.277
Under the Affordable Care Act she may stay on his

00:00:10.277 --> 00:00:14.229
plan until she turns 26, regardless of whether she is

00:00:14.229 --> 00:00:17.787
a student, married, financially dependent or living at home.

00:00:17.787 --> 00:00:22.925
Maryland law separately requires coverage of unmarried child dependents to age 25; the

00:00:22.925 --> 00:00:28.063
federal rule governs plans subject to it, and the more generous rule applies.

00:00:28.063 --> 00:00:33.202
When she reaches 26 she loses eligibility, which is a qualifying event for

00:00:33.202 --> 00:00:38.340
COBRA or Maryland continuation and a special enrollment opportunity on Maryland Health Connection.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:45.688
Non-grandfathered plans must cover recommended preventive services with no deductible, copayment or coinsurance when

00:00:45.688 --> 00:00:52.510
delivered in network: screenings and counseling rated A or B by the U.S.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.709
Preventive Services Task Force, recommended immunizations, and the

00:00:56.709 --> 00:01:00.383
preventive care guidelines for women and children.

00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:06.156
Elena’s mammogram and the children’s vaccines cost nothing out of pocket.

00:01:06.156 --> 00:01:11.404
Plans may not deny coverage, exclude a condition or charge

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:16.652
more because of a pre-existing condition, for adults or children.

00:01:16.652 --> 00:01:24.000
The HIPAA exclusion periods you learned in Lesson 24 are gone from comprehensive coverage.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.926
Before the ACA, some insurers canceled coverage retroactively when

00:01:27.926 --> 00:01:31.852
a member got sick, hunting the application for errors.

00:01:31.852 --> 00:01:36.214
Rescission is now permitted only for fraud or an intentional

00:01:36.214 --> 00:01:40.576
misrepresentation of a material fact, and the insurer must give

00:01:40.576 --> 00:01:44.501
30 days’ advance notice so the member can appeal.

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.682
Honest mistakes cannot cost coverage.

00:01:46.682 --> 00:01:50.608
Plans also may not impose lifetime dollar limits on

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:54.534
essential health benefits, or annual dollar limits on them.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:58.896
A plan may still limit non-essential benefits and may use

00:01:58.896 --> 00:02:02.822
visit limits that are not dollar caps where permitted.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:07.620
The result is that catastrophic illness no longer exhausts a policy.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:12.372
A plan that existed on March 23, 2010 and has

00:02:12.372 --> 00:02:17.124
not made significant changes, such as cutting benefits, raising coinsurance,

00:02:17.124 --> 00:02:21.401
or sharply increasing deductibles or employee contributions, is grandfathered.

00:02:21.401 --> 00:02:27.104
Grandfathered plans must still cover children to 26, drop lifetime limits and

00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:32.806
stop rescissions, but they are exempt from some rules: free preventive care,

00:02:32.806 --> 00:02:38.033
essential health benefits, the new appeals process and the rating limits.

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:39.934
Each year fewer remain.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:44.686
Once a plan loses grandfathered status it cannot regain it.

00:02:44.686 --> 00:02:48.963
Marcus’s employer plan lost its status when it doubled

00:02:48.963 --> 00:02:53.240
the deductible, so it now meets every ACA rule.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:59.914
Individual and small group plans must cover ten categories of essential health benefits.

00:02:59.914 --> 00:03:01.454
Ambulatory patient services.

00:03:01.454 --> 00:03:02.481
Emergency services.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:02.995
Hospitalization.

00:03:02.995 --> 00:03:05.048
Maternity and newborn care.

00:03:05.048 --> 00:03:10.696
Mental health and substance use disorder services, including behavioral health treatment.

00:03:10.696 --> 00:03:11.722
Prescription drugs.

00:03:11.722 --> 00:03:14.803
Rehabilitative and habilitative services and devices.

00:03:14.803 --> 00:03:15.830
Laboratory services.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:19.937
Preventive and wellness services and chronic disease management.

00:03:19.937 --> 00:03:23.531
Pediatric services, including oral and vision care.

00:03:23.531 --> 00:03:28.151
Each state picks a benchmark plan that defines the

00:03:28.151 --> 00:03:32.259
details; Maryland’s benchmark folds in the state mandates.

00:03:32.259 --> 00:03:37.906
Large group plans are not required to cover all ten but

00:03:37.906 --> 00:03:43.040
may not put dollar limits on any they do cover.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.408
Run Marcus’s family through the rules.

00:03:45.408 --> 00:03:47.776
The 24-year-old stays on the plan.

00:03:47.776 --> 00:03:50.144
Preventive visits are free in network.

00:03:50.144 --> 00:03:53.695
The younger child’s asthma cannot be excluded or surcharged.

00:03:53.695 --> 00:03:57.642
If Marcus forgot to list a decade-old prescription on an

00:03:57.642 --> 00:04:01.193
application, the plan cannot rescind for an honest omission.

00:04:01.193 --> 00:04:04.745
A 400,000 dollar hospital bill cannot exhaust a lifetime

00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:07.902
maximum, because there is none on essential benefits.

00:04:07.902 --> 00:04:11.059
And because his employer’s plan is no longer

00:04:11.059 --> 00:04:13.822
grandfathered, every one of these protections applies.

00:04:13.822 --> 00:04:17.768
Lesson 27 turns to the parts of the law that

00:04:17.768 --> 00:04:21.320
shape the marketplace: metal levels, appeals, subsidies and penalties.
